For projects requiring a more customized execution environment, Pipeline also supports building and running a container from a `Dockerfile` in the source repository. In contrast to the [previous approach](https://www.jenkins.io/doc/book/pipeline/docker/#execution-environment) of using an "off-the-shelf" container, using the `agent { dockerfile true }` syntax builds a new image from a `Dockerfile`, rather than pulling one from 
Reusing an example from above, with a more custom `Dockerfile`:
Dockerfile
```
